    "explanation": "A catalog-svc reconciler session opened transaction 88973 on catalog-db and left it open holding a row lock on products (line 128). Subsequent updates queued behind that lock (lines 140, 150), so catalog-svc's queries hit their statement timeout and search-api's calls to catalog-svc timed out (lines 146, 147, 152, 153, 170, 171). search-api's connection pool to catalog-svc saturating (lines 169, 176, 183) and the web-bff 504s (lines 168, 180, 187, 189, 198, 208, 212) are downstream symptoms. The fix is to kill the idle-in-transaction session, not to add capacity. Red herrings: lines 72, 73 (a single translation API connection reset that succeeded on retry, minutes before onset).",
